  "body": "## The gap\n\nv5.25.0 shipped `anthropic_oauth` with everything it needs in Python — credential discovery, PKCE login, refresh — and wired **only a CLI command**. `admin.js` contained **zero** references to it, so from the dashboard the provider was unreachable: no way to see whether a Claude Code credential existed, no way to import it, no way to sign in.\n\n`chatgpt_oauth` already solves exactly this, so the shape is **mirrored rather than invented** — a manifest pseudo-field renders the controls, the endpoints sit beside their ChatGPT counterparts, and the paste-code flow behaves the same.\n\n## What the card does now\n\n- **Use Claude Code credentials** — enabled only when `~/.claude/.credentials.json` is actually present, and shows a masked summary before you commit.\n- **Sign in with Anthropic** — the PKCE flow, opening the authorize URL and taking the pasted code.\n- A status line for the real state: none / imported / signed in / expired.\n\n## Three things this had to get right\n\nEach has a test that was broken on purpose and confirmed to fail **by name**:\n\n| | Guard |\n| --- | --- |\n| **`~/.claude/.credentials.json` is read-only to MCC** | snapshots the file's bytes and mtime under a redirected `HOME`, runs the import, asserts neither moved |\n| **No raw token in a response body** | asserts the secret appears *nowhere* in the response — not just in the field someone remembered to mask |\n| **The disclaimer is on the card, before either button** | asserts the warning renders as a warning |\n\nImport means *read, then write into MCC's own store*. Claude Code's file is never written and never refreshed in place.\n\nThe disclaimer matters because this provider uses a subscription credential in a way Anthropic's published policy forbids for third-party tools, and the only thing between a user and an account-level consequence is that the product says so:\n\n> Anthropic does not permit routing requests through Free, Pro, or Max plan credentials in third-party tools, and this provider additionally refuses any request that does not report `cc_entrypoint=cli`.\n\nIt reuses the existing `guide-note-warn` class rather than inventing one — which the asset-wiring guard added earlier this week would otherwise have failed.\n\n## Import boundary\n\n`api` may not import a provider package directly, so the edge is registered in `IMPORT_EXCEPTIONS` with the same `Owner:`/`Reason:` annotations `chatgpt_oauth` uses — the documented mechanism, not a bypass.\n\n## Verification\n\n**6 failed, 4388 passed, 26 skipped** vs baseline `6 failed, 4377 passed` on unmodified `fork/main` in the same shell — same six PowerShell installer failures, **+11 tests, zero regressions**. ruff format, ruff check, ty: clean.\n\nIndependently confirmed on review that `claude_credentials_path()` appears only in read and message paths, never in a writer.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n**No real Anthropic OAuth login was attempted.** The exchange is mocked, so the browser-open and paste-code round trip has never run against live Anthropic infrastructure. That was true of the provider when it shipped and remains true now — the UI makes the flow reachable, it does not prove Anthropic accepts it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
