    },
    "message": "feat(anthropic): sign in or import Claude Code credentials from the dashboard\n\nv5.25.0 shipped the anthropic_oauth provider with everything it needs in\nPython -- credential discovery, PKCE login, refresh -- and wired only a CLI\ncommand. admin.js contained zero references to it, so from the dashboard the\nprovider was unreachable: no way to see whether a Claude Code credential\nexisted, no way to import it, no way to sign in. The owner found it.\n\nchatgpt_oauth already solves exactly this, so the shape is mirrored rather\nthan invented: a manifest pseudo-field renders the controls, the endpoints\nsit beside their ChatGPT counterparts, and the paste-code flow behaves the\nsame way.\n\nThe card now offers two paths and says what state it is in. \"Use Claude Code\ncredentials\" is enabled only when the file is actually there, and shows a\nmasked summary before the user commits to anything. \"Sign in with Anthropic\"\nruns the PKCE flow and takes the pasted code.\n\nThree things this had to get right, each with a test that was broken on\npurpose and confirmed to fail by name:\n\n- ~/.claude/.credentials.json is READ-ONLY to MCC. Import means read, then\n  write into MCC's own store; Claude Code's file is never written and never\n  refreshed in place. The guard snapshots the file's bytes and mtime under a\n  redirected HOME, runs the import, and asserts neither moved.\n- No raw token reaches a response body. The sources endpoint reports masked\n  values only, and the guard asserts the secret appears nowhere in the\n  response rather than only in the field somebody remembered to mask.\n- The disclaimer is on the card, before either button. This provider uses a\n  subscription credential in a way Anthropic's published policy forbids for\n  third-party tools, and the only thing between a user and an account-level\n  consequence is that the product says so. It reuses the existing\n  guide-note-warn class rather than inventing one, which the asset-wiring\n  guard added earlier this week would have failed.\n\napi may not import a provider package directly, so the edge is registered in\nIMPORT_EXCEPTIONS with the same Owner:/Reason: annotations chatgpt_oauth uses\n-- the documented mechanism, not a bypass.\n\nVerification: full suite 6 failed, 4388 passed, 26 skipped against a baseline\nof 6 failed, 4377 passed on unmodified fork/main in the same shell. The same\nsix PowerShell installer failures, +11 tests, zero regressions. ruff format,\nruff check, ty clean. Confirmed independently that claude_credentials_path()\nappears only in read and message paths, never in a writer.\n\nNot verified: no real Anthropic OAuth login was attempted. The exchange is\nmocked, so the browser-open and paste-code round trip has never run against\nlive Anthropic infrastructure. That was true of the provider when it shipped\nand remains true now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
